T2 was scoped out when its premise was true (sibling unbound, no parity harness). Both
conditions expired, so the re-scope is reversed with the reason recorded rather than the
item quietly reappearing.

The record states what the binding is and is not: the interpreter already fetched through
the governed Tor-or-refuse path and codegen had no lowering at all, so this removes a silent
fallback and adds no capability and no egress-policy change. It also records the flipped
return shape, the by-name field reads, and the coercion defect fixed in both crawler arms.

Scope is stated rather than implied: from_links gets the full pinned-reference parity
because it plans offline; from_sitemap fetches, so its happy path cannot be exercised
offline and is left UNVERIFIED rather than claimed.

Separately, and outside this plan: `cargo test --lib runtime::` is red on a clean checkout
because of a bare `ureq::get` at crates/tallow-locator/src/watchers.rs:356 — unproxied, so
it would egress from the box IP, which the tree's own guard exists to prevent. The file is
untouched by this work and last changed 2026-09-28. Recorded with the site and why the fix
is not obviously local; not patched under a scraper task.
